# A known bug (../../RESULTS.md, "One server: the table metadata after a power cut";
# ClickHouse issue #111348, open, and its pull request #111405). Build ../hydo-metadata.yaml.
# The power goes off right after ClickHouse answered EXCHANGE TABLES a AND b, about a second
# after it answered ALTER TABLE t ADD COLUMN d. DatabaseAtomic swaps each table's new metadata
# file into place with renameat2(RENAME_EXCHANGE) and does not sync the folder, so the recovery
# boot loads the old files: the column d is gone and a holds 'a' again. metadata_kept fails
# ("the acknowledged ADD COLUMN d is gone; the acknowledged EXCHANGE TABLES is undone (a holds
# 'a')"), fingerprint 86516e86259630a9 on hvx with the image dd365579233483cf.
#   hydo run <image> "$(tail -1 alter-and-exchange-undone-after-power-cut.schedule)"
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=cut | run C=2
